# Tailored resumes (`<Person>_<Company>_<Role>_resume.tex`) vs master (`complete/master-resume.tex`)

Tailored packets live under **`people/<Person>/<CompanySlug>/<RoleSlug>/`** (company folder, then role folder). LaTeX/PDF names use **`<Person>_<Company>_<Role>`** as the stem, for example `Ali-Syed-Ayan_Creaxon-Technologies_Software-Engineer-HK_resume.tex` in `people/Ali-Syed-Ayan/Creaxon-Technologies/Software-Engineer-HK/`. See `scripts/layout_paths.py` (`job_packet_dir`, `tailored_packet_basename`, `tailored_resume_tex`, `tailored_cover_letter_tex`).

Each **role** folder must also include **`job link.txt`** (exact name, including the space): a plain-text file whose **first line** is the **canonical job posting URL** the user supplied (LinkedIn, company careers page, or other). Prefer a short, stable URL without tracking query junk when the user provides both; mirror the same URL in the top-of-file `%` comment on `<Person>_<Company>_<Role>_resume.tex` when applicable. Update `job link.txt` whenever the posting link changes. You can (re)write it with `python scripts/generate_job_package.py --person <Person> --company <CompanySlug> --role <RoleSlug> --job-url "<URL>"` before or after compiling.

## What runs automatically (Cursor)

- **This project rule** is attached when **any** file matching **`globs`** in the frontmatter is **open or in context** (you are editing it, or it is part of the current task). You do **not** need to name the rule.
- **Skills** (under `.cursor/skills/`) are **not** the same: they load when **explicitly invoked** or when Cursor matches them by description; they are **not** guaranteed every turn. **All Zhao Yanbo resume rules that matter for editing are in this file**; the optional skill file is only a short pointer for people browsing the skills list.

