## Scope

- **`people/<Person>/complete/master-resume.tex`**: May exceed **one page** when content requires it.
- **`people/<Person>/<CompanySlug>/<RoleSlug>/<Person>_<CompanySlug>_<RoleSlug>_resume.tex`**: Must compile to **exactly one PDF page** whenever feasible.

## Punctuation, typography, and STAR bullets

Applies to **resume and cover letter prose** in all paths matched by this rule’s `globs` (tailored packets, masters when open, and cover letters).

### Punctuation

- **Parentheses:** Use **sparingly**; only when they remove real ambiguity (for example a precise legal title). Prefer **commas**, **colons**, and **semicolons** to stack clauses or short lists inside an `\item`.
- **Em dash:** Do **not** use an em dash (`---` in LaTeX or a Unicode em dash in source) as sentence punctuation. Prefer a **comma**, **colon**, **semicolon**, or a tighter rewrite.
- **Hyphens:** Use **hyphens** for standard compounds and for **clear date spans** in headings (`Sept.\ 2023 -- Jun.\ 2024`, `Jun.\ 2022 -- Jun.\ 2026`). Use **commas** or **hyphenated phrasing** for “which team / division” inside a title line instead of decorative dash pairs.
- **Tilde / approximation:** Do **not** use `~` in prose or `$\sim$` for “approximately”; write **about** or **approximately** before the number or percent.

### STAR bullets

- Each `\item` should read as a **condensed STAR** story: lead with a **strong action verb**; fold **Situation** and **Task** into a short phrase; show **Actions** you owned (tools, partners); end with a **quantified Result** when the master supports it (hours, percent, latency, volume, cost).
- Keep each bullet to **at most two wrapped lines** in the PDF. Do **not** paste long duty paragraphs.

**Ali Syed Ayan tone reference:** When editing Ali’s materials, align rhythm and metric placement with **`people/Ali-Syed-Ayan/complete/Syed Ayan Ali Resume 2026.pdf`** (or **`g:\My Drive\Syed Ayan Ali Resume 2026.pdf`** when available), without inventing facts beyond `people/Ali-Syed-Ayan/complete/master-resume.tex` and `resume-knowledge-base.yaml`.

## Hyperlinks (clickable PDF)

Use **`hyperref`** `\href{URL}{visible text}` anywhere a URL should be clickable in the exported PDF. Match the **spirit** of the 2026 one-pager (`people/Ali-Syed-Ayan/complete/Syed Ayan Ali Resume 2026.pdf` or `g:\My Drive\Syed Ayan Ali Resume 2026.pdf`): contact channels and any documented product or chatbot links appear as real links, not plain text.

### Contact block and cover letters

- **Email:** `\href{mailto:local-part@domain}{local-part@domain}` (or the same address in the visible text).
- **GitHub, LinkedIn, portfolio:** `\href{https://...}{...}` using the **exact** URLs from that person’s `complete/resume-knowledge-base.yaml` and/or `complete/master-resume.tex`. Prefer short labels in the second argument (`GitHub`, `LinkedIn`) when it still matches the reference layout; otherwise use the full URL as visible text if the user’s template does.
- **Job posting (cover letter):** For **Ali Syed Ayan** tailored `*_cover-letter.tex`, **do not** link the posting by LinkedIn job ID or `\href` to the job URL in the letter body. Name the **company** and **role** in plain text only. The posting URL still belongs in that packet’s **`job link.txt`** and in `%` comments at the top of the `.tex` file for traceability.

### Ali Syed Ayan tailored cover letters

When editing `people/Ali-Syed-Ayan/<CompanySlug>/<RoleSlug>/*_cover-letter.tex`:

- **Length:** Keep the **entire letter** at or below **250 words** from salutation through sign-off when you count the visible prose, not LaTeX commands.
- **Opening:** After `Dear Hiring Manager,`, the **first paragraph** must **state plainly** what you are applying for and put the **role title in bold** using `\textbf{...}` once. Include **company name** and location in text. **No** LinkedIn job reference numbers or posting links in the body.
- **Body:** Follow with a short paragraph that ties your background to the role, then **exactly three** `\item` lines in an `itemize` list. Each item should lead with a **short bold label**, a **colon**, then one dense sentence that maps to the job description and includes **quantified** outcomes where the master supports them, for example hours saved, percent change, latency, revenue context, or monthly cost removed.
- **Regulated or delivery-heavy work:** Include at least one clear sentence, in prose or inside a bullet, that you have thrived in **high stakes, delivery focused** settings and can bring that discipline to the employer.
- **Sign-off:** End with `Warm Regards,` then a blank line, then `Syed Ayan Ali` as the printed name, not `Sincerely` or `Ali Syed Ayan` unless the user asks otherwise.
- **Tone:** Conversational but authoritative, professional, not stiff. Use **contractions** where they sound natural. Vary sentence length. Prefer simple, active verbs. **Do not** use stock AI phrases such as “unlock the potential,” “delve,” “tapestry,” “in summary,” “let’s explore,” “fostering,” or “game changer.”
- **Punctuation habits:** Avoid decorative hyphen chains, em dashes, stacked parentheses, backslashes used to stack examples, and **excessive** colons outside the three list items. The three bullets are the main place colons should appear.

### Deliverables (chatbots, sites, demos)

- When the **master**, **YAML**, or the user’s **2026 PDF template** already records a **stable URL** for work you describe (e.g. a public site, a documented chatbot or app link, a dashboard), **repeat that URL** in the matching experience or project bullet using `\href{URL}{name or hostname}`. Example already in Ali’s master: `\href{https://hkmrs.org}{hkmrs.org}`.
- **Do not** invent, guess, or shorten URLs in ways that break the link. If no URL exists in those sources, keep the achievement text **without** a fake link.

## Layout

- **Ali Syed Ayan:** Start from **`people/Ali-Syed-Ayan/complete/template-resume.tex`** for `\documentclass`, `\usepackage` (including **`geometry`**), `\setlength{\parskip}`, `\ressection`, `\resumeSubheading`, `\resumeHeading`, **`itemize`** (`enumitem`), and header block structure. Pull factual bullet content from the master and YAML, not the master’s preamble.
- **Everyone else (e.g. Zhao Yanbo):** Start from the **same** preamble as that person’s **`complete/master-resume.tex`**: `\documentclass`, `\usepackage` lines (including **`geometry`** margins), `\setlength{\parskip}`, `\ressection`, `\resumeSubheading`, `\resumeHeading`, and **`itemize`** (`enumitem`) settings.

### Pagination vs completeness

- **Do not** tighten margins, `\parskip`, list `itemsep`, or macro vertical skips relative to that person’s **reference preamble** (`complete/master-resume.tex` for Zhao-style packets; `people/Ali-Syed-Ayan/complete/template-resume.tex` for Ali Syed Ayan) just to force one page.
- If **one page is impossible** while keeping **every** master `Work Experience` entry **and** an unchanged reference preamble, **stop** and tell the user. Practical outs (pick one after user confirms):
  - Omit the **oldest** role **only** when the user explicitly allows it for that packet, **or**
  - Accept **two pages** for that tailored packet, **or**
  - The user agrees to a **documented** one-off preamble tweak (discouraged).

When an oldest role is omitted for pagination, add a **short `%` comment** above `\ressection{Extracurricular Activities}` explaining why.

## Section headings (fixed labels)

Always include these three headings **verbatim**:

1. **`Work Experience`**
2. **`Extracurricular Activities`**
3. **`Skills \& Other Information`**

Do **not** rename or merge these sections.

## Work experience entries

- Copy **the same employers, titles, locations, and date ranges** as the master resume (**same date formatting**, e.g. `Sept.\ 2023`, `Jun.\ 2024`, `Present`).
- **Do not** drop or reorder roles **unless** (a) the user explicitly asks to remove or rewrite the **last** listed role, or (b) the pagination rule above applies and the user approves omitting the oldest entry.
- Tailoring for a job ad is done **only inside bullet points**, weaving in keywords from the posting **without** inventing employers, titles, dates, degrees, or credentials.

### Bullet counts (Zhao Yanbo; pagination fallback for Ali)

- **Two most recent roles** (first two blocks under Work Experience): **exactly 3** bullets each.
- **Every other role**: **at least 2** bullets each.

**Ali Syed Ayan:** Do **not** treat the above counts as the default. Follow **Ali Syed Ayan: job posting, keywords, and bullet selection** in the Exception block. Apply **3 / ≥2** caps only when trimming a **multi-page** Ali tailored PDF, together with the **Workflow after edits** steps below.

### Bullet shape

- Aim for **at most two wrapped lines per bullet** in the PDF (concise prose).
- **Two-line density:** If a bullet **wraps to two lines**, the second line must **earn its space**; add real substance (metric, scope, control, stakeholder, or tool) so it reads as a **full** second line, not a **short orphan** with lots of empty measure below. If you cannot justify a full second line honestly, **collapse** the bullet to **one** strong **one-liner** instead of paying a line for half a line of value.
- Prefer strong ops/markets language aligned with the posting (e.g. trade lifecycle, booking, settlement, operational risk, STP, downstream Risk/Finance, escalation).

## Education

- Mirror the master resume’s education `\resumeSubheading` rows (schools, degree lines with honours/GPA, dates).

## Extracurricular Activities

- Keep **each activity** as its own `\resumeHeading{...}{...}` with `\begin{itemize}...\end{itemize}` underneath (**≥1 bullet per activity**). Preserve the **master wording** when the tailored PDF already fits **one page**; if pagination still fails after compressing **Work Experience**, you may **shorten extracurricular bullets** (same facts, fewer words) **before** touching **Skills \& Other Information** line items.

## Skills \& Other Information

Use **exactly three** `\item` lines:

1. `\textbf{Languages:} ...`
2. `\textbf{IT skills:} ...`
3. `\textbf{Interests:} ...`

Keep labels identical; body text should match the master unless the user requests edits.

## Workflow after edits

Compile via `scripts/generate_job_package.py --person … --company … --role …` (or the project `pdflatex` helper). When the user supplies a posting URL for a packet, keep **`job link.txt`** in the **role** folder updated (line 1 = URL) or pass **`--job-url "<URL>"`** to the script. If the PDF is **longer than one page**, paginate in this order (still **no** margin or list-spacing cheats):

1. **Introduce 2-3 one-liner bullets** across the resume: pick bullets that are long or wrap badly (often **older / less posting-relevant** `Work Experience` roles, or **Extracurricular** bullets) and rewrite each as a **single dense line** in the PDF. Spread these **2-3** edits across sections so you do not strip only one block unless one pass is enough.
2. If the PDF is **still** longer than one page after recompiling, treat that as **consistently** over length: in the **least posting-relevant** area (weakest bullet in the oldest or farthest-from-role `Work Experience` block, or a peripheral Education/Extracurricular bullet), **cut that bullet’s verbose text** and **replace the same `\item` slot** with **one** **one-liner** that keeps the strongest verifiable fact or keyword. Repeat sparingly toward more relevant bullets, without dropping below **minimum bullet counts** unless the user approved an exception (e.g. omitting the oldest role). **For Ali Syed Ayan**, once length pressure is clear, you may also enforce **at most 3** bullets for each of the **two** most recent roles and **at least 2** for other retained roles **as part of the same trimming pass**, after keyword-rich bullets have been tried first.

Stop when the tailored PDF is **exactly one page** (verify in the `.log` “Output written … (1 page …)” line).
